    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d674">

                <pb facs="0987" n="867" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg867"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.00/8: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Schurman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-12-06T16:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 6,
                                1922—4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 5:25 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>480. My telegram 466, November 29, 4 p.m. International commission consists of
                    American and British military attaches and French, Italian and Japanese, Chinese
                    secretaries, Cheney<anchor n="36" xml:id="d674-f1"/> president by seniority.</p>
                <p>General Wu Pei-fu replied to commission’s telegram<anchor n="37" xml:id="d674-f2"
                    /> expressing regrets at his failure to effect release captured foreigners,
                    alleging progress and suggesting on that account “coming of commission might
                    perhaps be deferred.” Foreign Office covering note 4th and unperfected treaty
                    representations press same suggestion.</p>
                <pb facs="0988" n="868" xml:id="pg868"/>
                <p>Diplomatic body met to-day to consider matter. All approved postponing
                    commission’s departure from 7th to 14th. I suggested our resolution should state
                    such action taken not only at request of Wu and Foreign Office but also in view
                    of announcement new Cabinet December 10 and this was adopted.</p>
                <p>From absolutely reliable sources we learn Wu was very angry at publication
                    diplomatic body’s telegram<anchor n="38" xml:id="d674-f3"/> holding him jointly
                    responsible for continued captivity of foreigners and denounced Foreign Office
                    for sending it to him integrally instead of in abstract.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Schurman</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
